.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_SHA1 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_sha1
.Nd SHA-1 For EVP
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft const EVP_MD *
.Fo EVP_sha1
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
SHA-1 (Secure Hash Algorithm 1) is a cryptographic hash function
standardized in NIST FIPS 180-4. The algorithm was designed by the
United States National Security Agency and initially published in 1995.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_sha1()
The SHA-1 algorithm which produces a 160-bit output from a given input.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling this function multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_MD_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_MD-SHA1 7
instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return a
.Sy EVP_MD
structure that contains the implementation of the message digest.
See
.Xr EVP_MD_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_MD
structure.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
NIST FIPS 180-4.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr evp 7 ,
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
